<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jezebel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jezebel was a Phoenician princess, the daughter of Ethbaal, king of the Sidonians, who married King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab of Israel</a> in the ninth century BCE. The Books of Kings portray her as a promoter of the worship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baal">Baal</a> and an enemy of the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elijah">Elijah</a>, and tell how she was thrown from a window at Jezreel on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>'s orders after his coup. Her name became a byword for a wicked woman.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jezebel.jpg" alt="Jezebel" width="320" height="587" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Byam Liston Shaw · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Liston_Byam_Shaw_003.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
